# Tier 6 — Full Physical Memory / RAM

**Highly volatile**

RAM can disappear completely when power is removed and substantial portions can change while the machine continues operating.

When authorized and technically possible:

* [ ] Acquire a complete physical memory image.
* [ ] Record acquisition tool.
* [ ] Record tool version.
* [ ] Record acquisition start time.
* [ ] Record acquisition completion time.
* [ ] Record destination media.
* [ ] Record acquisition errors.
* [ ] Calculate cryptographic hashes of the resulting image.
* [ ] Preserve the original memory acquisition.
* [ ] Analyze a working copy.

Memory may contain evidence of:

* [ ] Running processes
* [ ] Terminated process remnants
* [ ] Process command lines
* [ ] Network connections
* [ ] Injected code
* [ ] Unpacked malware
* [ ] Reflectively loaded code
* [ ] DLLs / shared libraries
* [ ] Kernel modules
* [ ] Drivers
* [ ] Encryption keys
* [ ] Credentials
* [ ] Authentication material
* [ ] Kerberos tickets
* [ ] Browser session material
* [ ] Clipboard contents
* [ ] Command history remnants
* [ ] Console buffers
* [ ] Decrypted content
* [ ] File-system structures
* [ ] Registry structures
* [ ] Environment variables
* [ ] Shellcode
* [ ] Rootkits
* [ ] Memory-only malware

### Critical decision

If full-disk encryption is active and the system is currently unlocked, shutting the system down before memory acquisition may make subsequent evidence acquisition substantially more difficult.

That decision must be made deliberately and documented.

